{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgGCXxWtieQXMam5cQRz6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking \"What is the status bar bug, and how do I fix it?\" The status strip is a black bar on the welcome and error frames. The instance fill was set to white, but the parent is white, so a white fill is consistent with the splash showing a white strip and the welcome showing black only if paint() overwrote the instance root fill inconsistently. The robust fix is to stop using status bar instances and build my own status bar with dark and light variants, then place those. The home indicator looks fine and stays as is. The \"Create account\" label is clipped: the instance shows a tiny pill about 70 wide instead of 354x60, so I set instance.resize(354, 60) explicitly and layoutSizingHorizontal='FIXED'. The error icon overlaps the message text, so I place the text at x=30 after the field with no icon. The password eye icon sits oddly, so I omit it. On the welcome frame the hero illustration shows a white background rect, which is acceptable. The splash logo has a white background, so I place it on a 240x159 white rounded-24 tile to look intentional. For the status bar I create two 414x44 variants, one light and one dark, drawing the 9:41 text, signal bars, wifi and battery simply. Home is 414x932: portfolio card at y=140, 366x196, source text \"Your total asset portfolio\", \"₦203,935\", pill \"+2%\", \"vs last month\"; plans row at y=340 holds 3 cards of 112 wide with 15 gaps (24+112*3+2*15=366); article rows sit from y=545 to 830; tab bar at 848. The overlay sheet starts at y=180 with a rounded top of 32.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":2520,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":61749,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2520}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e88086fc-1add-4fb7-8fa0-ba5b7cccc2de","uuid":"17c347fe-7105-4f4c-aadf-5bd81570cc41","timestamp":"2026-10-28T18:49:54.621Z","thinking_duration_ms":36801}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgGCXxWtieQXMam5cQRz6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixing what I see: the supplied status bar instances render as a black strip, the primary button instance collapsed to a tiny pill, and the error message overlaps its icon. I'll build my own status bar components, then add the remaining six screens plus shared header/row components in one pass."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":2520,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":61749,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2520}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e88086fc-1add-4fb7-8fa0-ba5b7cccc2de","uuid":"b03314eb-9bb8-4c73-94d1-303735a4763d","timestamp":"2026-10-28T18:49:56.375Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgGCXxWtieQXMam5cQRz6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012kxV4c4jjoivArALmLuOgs","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"code":"const ws = figma.root.children.find(p=>p.name.indexOf('03 · Workspace')===0);\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(ws);\nconst F={fr:{family:'Inter',style:'Regular'},fm:{family:'Inter',style:'Medium'},fs:{family:'Inter',style:'Semi Bold'},fb:{family:'Inter',style:'Bold'},dr:{family:'DM Sans',style:'Regular'},dm:{family:'DM Sans',style:'Medium'},ds:{family:'DM Sans',style:'SemiBold'},db:{family:'DM Sans',style:'Bold'}};\nfor(const k in F) await figma.loadFontAsync(F[k]);\nconst C={primary:'#31A062',primaryDark:'#26814F',primarySoft:'#E7F4EC',ink:'#12211A',ink2:'#5B6B63',ink3:'#8A988F',line:'#E7EDE9',surface:'#F4F7F5',white:'#FFFFFF',dark:'#0C2A1B',dark2:'#123A26',danger:'#D93F3F',dangerSoft:'#FDECEC',gold:'#E4B23C'};\nfunction rgb(h){h=h.replace('#','');return {r:parseInt(h.slice(0,2),16)/255,g:parseInt(h.slice(2,4),16)/255,b:parseInt(h.slice(4,6),16)/255};}\nfunction solid(h,op){return {type:'SOLID',color:rgb(h),opacity:op===undefined?1:op};}\nfunction fr(name,w,h,fill,r,x,y){const f=figma.createFrame();f.name=name;f.resize(w,h);f.fills=fill?[solid(fill)]:[];if(r){f.cornerRadius=r;}f.clipsContent=true;f.x=x||0;f.y=y||0;return f;}\nfunction tx(parent,name,str,font,size,lh,color,x,y,w,align){const t=figma.createText();t.name=name;t.fontName=font;t.fontSize=size;t.lineHeight={unit:'PIXELS',value:lh};t.characters=str;t.fills=[solid(color)];if(w){t.textAutoResize='HEIGHT';t.resize(w,10);if(align)t.textAlignHorizontal=align;parent.appendChild(t);t.x=x;t.y=y;}else{parent.appendChild(t);if(x!==undefined){t.x=x;t.y=y;}}return t;}\nfunction rect(parent,name,w,h,fill,r,x,y,stroke,sw){const e=figma.createRectangle();e.name=name;e.resize(w,h);e.cornerRadius=r||0;e.fills=fill?[solid(fill)]:[];if(stroke){e.strokes=[solid(stroke)];e.strokeWeight=sw||1;e.strokeAlign='INSIDE';}parent.appendChild(e);e.x=x||0;e.y=y||0;return e;}\nfunction el(parent,name,w,h,fill,x,y,stroke,sw){const e=figma.createEllipse();e.name=name;e.resize(w,h);e.fills=fill?[solid(fill)]:[];if(stroke){e.strokes=[solid(stroke)];e.strokeWeight=sw||1;}parent.appendChild(e);e.x=x;e.y=y;return e;}\nfunction img(name,w,h,hash,mode){const r=figma.createRectangle();r.name=name;r.resize(w,h);r.fills=[{type:'IMAGE',imageHash:hash,scaleMode:mode||'FILL'}];return r;}\nfunction icon(name,parent,x,y,color,scale){const m=figma.getNodeById(name);const inst=m.createInstance();inst.name='Icon';if(scale)inst.rescale(scale);const paint=(n)=>{if(n.type==='GROUP'||n.type==='FRAME'){if('children'in n)n.children.forEach(paint);return;}if('strokes'in n&&n.strokes&&n.strokes.length)n.strokes=[solid(color)];if('fills'in n&&n.fills&&n.fills.length)n.fills=[solid(color)];if('children'in n)n.children.forEach(paint);};paint(inst);parent.appendChild(inst);inst.x=x;inst.y=y;return inst;}\n// ---------- status bar components ----------\nconst SB={};\nfor(const dark of [false,true]){\n  const c=figma.createComponent(); c.name=dark?'Status Bar/Dark':'Status Bar/Light'; c.resize(414,44);\n  c.fills=[solid(dark?C.dark:C.white)];\n  const col=dark?C.white:C.ink;\n  tx(c,'9:41','9:41',F.fs,15,18,col,32,14,null);\n  for(let i=0;i<4;i++){const b=rect(c,'Bar'+(i+1),3,4+i*3,col,1.5,282+i*6,26-(4+i*3));}\n  el(c,'Wifi',14,11,null,312,23, col,1.6);\n  rect(c,'Battery',25,12,null,334,20,col,1.2).cornerRadius=3;\n  rect(c,'Fill',18,8,col,2,338,22).cornerRadius=1.5;\n  rect(c,'Cap',2,4,col,1,360,24);\n  c.x=1180; c.y=860+(dark?60:0);\n  SB[dark?'dark':'light']=c;\n}\nfunction statusBar(parent,dark){const inst=SB[dark?'dark':'light'].createInstance();inst.name='Status Bar';parent.appendChild(inst);inst.x=0;inst.y=0;return inst;}\nfunction homeIndicator(parent,dark){const c=rect(parent,'Home Indicator',134,5,dark?C.white:C.ink,3,140,911);c.opacity=dark?0.9:0.9;return c;}\nfunction navBtn(parent,x,y,iconId,gray){const b=fr('Icon Button',44,44,gray?C.surface:C.white,14,x,y);b.strokes=[solid(C.line)];b.strokeWeight=1;b.strokeAlign='INSIDE';const m=figma.getNodeById(iconId);const inst=icon(iconId,b,Math.round((44-m.width)/2),Math.round((44-m.height)/2),C.ink);return b;}\nfunction avatar(parent,x,y,d,label,bg){const a=el(parent,'Avatar',d,d,bg||C.primarySoft,x,y);tx(parent,'Avatar Initials',label||'JM',F.ds,Math.round(d*0.34),Math.round(d*0.42),C.primary,x,y+d*0.3,d,'CENTER');return a;}\nfunction sectionRow(parent,title,action,color){tx(parent,'Section '+title,title,F.ds,19,24,C.ink,24,0,200);if(action)tx(parent,'Action '+action,action,F.fm,13,18,C.primary,314,4,76,'RIGHT');}\n// fix existing frames: remove broken status bars\nconst allFrames=ws.children.filter(n=>n.type==='FRAME');\nfor(const f of allFrames){ for(const ch of [...f.children]){ if(ch.name==='Status Bar'){ ch.remove(); } if(ch.name==='Home Indicator'&&ch.type==='INSTANCE'){ch.remove();} } }\n// also clean welcome bad button? keep, will replace by checking width\nconst fixFrames=['2007:20','2007:41','2007:63','2007:93','2007:126'].map(id=>figma.getNodeById(id));\nfor(const f of fixFrames){\n  const dark=f.name==='01_Splash';\n  const sb=statusBar(f,dark); f.insertChild(0,sb); sb.x=0; sb.y=0;\n  if(!f.children.find(c=>c.name==='Home Indicator'&&c.type==='RECTANGLE')) homeIndicator(f,dark);\n  // remove trailing login row duplication? none\n}\n// remove broken error icon and reposition message\nconst ef=figma.getNodeById('2007:126');\nconst badIcon=ef.children.find(c=>c.name==='Error Icon'); if(badIcon) badIcon.remove();\nconst emsg=ef.children.find(c=>c.name==='Error msg'); if(emsg){emsg.x=30;emsg.y=540;}\n// ensure primary buttons are 354 wide\nfor(const f of fixFrames){ for(const ch of f.children){ if(ch.name==='Button · Create account'){ ch.resize(354,60); ch.x=30; ch.y=f.name==='02_Welcome'?748:740; } } }\n// welcome: tighten spacing, replace small pill\nconst wf=figma.getNodeById('2007: